   "id": 632218,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol start=\"1\">\n<li>&nbsp;<span>The scatter plot shows the number of times a player came to bat and the number of hits they had.</span><br>\n<img alt=\"A scatter plot. Horizontal, 0 to 600, by 50’s, labeled at bats. Vertical, 0 to 150, by 12 point 5’s, labeled hits. 19 dots trend linearly up and to the right.\" height=\"322\" src=\"exercises/media/e482d8e2020b8ec5.svg\" width=\"310\"><br></li>\n</ol>\n<div>\n    <p>The scatter plot includes a point at <span data-math=\"(318,80)\">(318,80)</span>. Describe the meaning of this point in this situation.</p>\n  </div>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1224130,
     "content_html": "For every 80 at bats, there are 318 hits."
    },
    {
     "id": 1224131,
     "content_html": "For every 318 at bats, there are 80 hits."
    }
   ],
